- [ ] `#[AllowBots]` attribute on controllers/actions to skip enforcement per action
- [ ] Verdict cache per fingerprint (skip re-evaluating signals for a known client)
- [ ] Tarpit reaction: delay then serve a minimal response (dangerous with php-fpm workers: each delayed request holds a worker)
- [ ] `RateSignal`: requests per minute per IP via `RateLimiter`
- [ ] `HoneypotSignal`: hit on a trap route / hidden form field no human sees
- [ ] Ban list: `bot_bans` table (ip or cidr, reason, expires_at), `bot-detector:ban` / `unban`, auto-ban after N automated verdicts in a window
- [ ] Signal: `Sec-CH-UA` Chromium major version differs from the UA major version
- [ ] Signal: `Sec-CH-UA-Platform` differs from the UA operating system
- [ ] Signal: `Accept: */*` on an HTML navigation, or `Accept-Language: *`
- [ ] Reactions per bot category (e.g. block only AI crawlers), using the Matomo category exposed on `Detection`
- [ ] `bot-detector:log-only` on a route inside a group that already runs `bot-detector` (e.g. `web`) is ignored: Laravel dedupes only identical names, so the plain instance enforces first. Fix: run once per request and let a route's `log-only` win (README documents the workaround: separate route groups)
